 R←Test_API_025(stopFlag batchFlag);⎕TRAP;tempDir;filename1;filename2;hash1;hash2;rc;msg;folder1;folder2
⍝ Runs "CompareVersions": checks that the two files it produces really do carry the two
⍝ versions the two commits are holding.
 ⎕TRAP←(999 'C' '. ⍝ Deliberate error')(0 'N')
 R←T._Failed
 folder1←folder2←''

 tempDir←FilesAndDirs.GetTempSubDir'APLGit2-Tests'
 (⊂'first')⎕NPUT tempDir,'/one.txt'
 {}∆Initialize tempDir
 (⊂'second')⎕NPUT(tempDir,'/one.txt')1
 {}tempDir G.U.RunGitCommand'add .'
 {}tempDir G.U.RunGitCommand'commit -m "Second commit"'

 ⍝ Without any hashes the two most recent commits must be taken:
 (filename1 filename2 hash1 hash2)←tempDir G.CompareVersions'./one.txt'
 folder1←⊃⎕NPARTS filename1

 →T.GoToTidyUp 0=≢filename1
 →T.GoToTidyUp 0=≢filename2
 →T.GoToTidyUp hash1≡hash2
 →T.GoToTidyUp'.txt'≢¯4↑filename1                     ⍝ The extension must survive
 →T.GoToTidyUp(,⊂'second')≢⊃⎕NGET filename1 1         ⍝ hash1 is the most recent commit
 →T.GoToTidyUp(,⊂'first')≢⊃⎕NGET filename2 1

 ⍝ The very same thing but with the two hashes specified explicitly, in reverse order:
 (filename1 filename2)←2↑tempDir G.CompareVersions'./one.txt'hash2 hash1
 folder2←⊃⎕NPARTS filename1
 →T.GoToTidyUp(,⊂'first')≢⊃⎕NGET filename1 1
 →T.GoToTidyUp(,⊂'second')≢⊃⎕NGET filename2 1

 R←T._OK

∆TidyUp:
 {}{0=≢⍵:0 ⋄ FilesAndDirs.RmDirByForce ⍵}¨folder1 folder2
 (rc msg)←FilesAndDirs.RmDirByForce tempDir
 msg Assert rc=0
⍝Done
